WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.388 --> 00:00:17.873
The flying painting hovered in the air along one wall of the gym.

2
00:00:19.773 --> 00:00:25.095
It showed a famous race, with witches zooming through a moonlit sky on sleek brooms.

3
00:00:26.575 --> 00:00:34.780
Some areas of the painting still looked beautiful, but Ben saw several long, messy smears across one section.

4
00:00:37.101 --> 00:00:43.407
In another spot, colors ran together, and little blobs of paint floated in the air all around the

5
00:00:43.447 --> 00:00:44.327
flying painting.

6
00:00:46.209 --> 00:00:48.651
A few witches stood looking at it in horror.

7
00:00:49.592 --> 00:00:51.773
Greta was chewing nervously on her hat.

8
00:00:51.793 --> 00:00:54.415
"After all that work!"

9
00:00:56.677 --> 00:00:57.398
she sobbed.

10
00:00:57.418 --> 00:00:59.640
"Our painting is ruined!"

11
00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:03.081
Ben stood helplessly beside Winnie.

12
00:01:06.644 --> 00:01:08.385
not that bad," he mumbled.

13
00:01:08.405 --> 00:01:14.668
"I mean, I know it's not perfect anymore, but—" Winnie shot him a look, and he stopped talking.

14
00:01:15.969 --> 00:01:19.852
Waldo burst into the room, his glasses flying off his face.

15
00:01:20.432 --> 00:01:21.693
"This is terrible!"

16
00:01:22.753 --> 00:01:24.434
He stooped to pick up his glasses.

17
00:01:24.454 --> 00:01:26.836
"Who ruined the painting?"

18
00:01:28.924 --> 00:01:30.745
Mr. Freaky spun toward Ben.

19
00:01:30.765 --> 00:01:34.027
"I think I know who the culprit is!"

20
00:01:35.068 --> 00:01:36.749
Several monsters gasped.

21
00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.031
Ben held up his hands.

22
00:01:40.051 --> 00:01:42.132
"I'm not the vandal, Mr.

23
00:01:42.192 --> 00:01:43.393
Freaky," he said.

24
00:01:43.413 --> 00:01:47.915
"As I was trying to tell you earlier, I had nothing to do with that missing painting.

25
00:01:48.576 --> 00:01:51.317
I had nothing to do with this mischief either."

26
00:01:52.158 --> 00:01:55.420
Mr. Freaky stared at Ben for a second before nodding.

27
00:01:57.032 --> 00:01:59.514
Then he slumped over, looking defeated.

28
00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:05.018
"Leonardo da Creepy will be here at seven," he moaned.

29
00:02:05.038 --> 00:02:08.040
"Art Week is totally out of control!

30
00:02:09.781 --> 00:02:11.302
What are we going to do?"

31
00:02:11.322 --> 00:02:16.286
"I know what we're going to do," Winnie said suddenly.

32
00:02:16.306 --> 00:02:17.867
"We're going to fix it.

33
00:02:18.407 --> 00:02:19.608
We have to anyway.

34
00:02:20.649 --> 00:02:25.132
Greta, round up as many sixth-grade witches as you can find," she commanded.

35
00:02:25.704 --> 00:02:29.886
"Samantha, see if you can locate the witches from the broom-flying squad."

36
00:02:30.727 --> 00:02:33.829
"Okay!" The two witches raced off on their brooms.

37
00:02:33.849 --> 00:02:37.571
"We need some new paints," Waldo said.

38
00:02:37.591 --> 00:02:38.931
"I'll start mixing them."

39
00:02:40.132 --> 00:02:42.353
"I can help you," another witch said.

40
00:02:42.373 --> 00:02:45.455
"I'm in Advanced Magic class this year."

41
00:02:46.376 --> 00:02:49.537
The two of them went into a corner of the gym to cast spells.

42
00:02:51.158 --> 00:02:53.940
While the other monsters worked, Ben looked for clues.

43
00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:59.738
Soon he spotted the gym teacher talking to Mr.

44
00:02:59.798 --> 00:03:06.241
Freaky. Gwarg, did you see anything suspicious?"

45
00:03:06.561 --> 00:03:07.282
Ben asked.

46
00:03:07.822 --> 00:03:09.263
Mr. Gwarg shrugged.

47
00:03:09.283 --> 00:03:13.845
"I did hear a commotion a little while ago.

48
00:03:14.486 --> 00:03:18.288
But when I got inside the gym, the painting had already been damaged.

49
00:03:19.088 --> 00:03:20.589
The gym was deserted."

50
00:03:23.771 --> 00:03:24.511
Ben sighed.

51
00:03:26.592 --> 00:03:28.193
"It looks like the vandal got away again."

52
00:03:28.213 --> 00:03:34.276
"That means he or she could try to ruin some of our artwork again," Mr.

53
00:03:34.316 --> 00:03:35.036
Freaky said.

54
00:03:35.056 --> 00:03:37.677
"I'd better go check on my sculpture."

55
00:03:37.697 --> 00:03:41.479
"And I'll patrol the halls," Mr.

56
00:03:41.539 --> 00:03:42.240
Gwarg said.

57
00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:46.301
"Ben, let me know if you discover any clues in here."

58
00:03:47.322 --> 00:03:51.264
Ben nodded and went to the painting to see if he could do anything to help.

59
00:03:53.688 --> 00:03:57.129
Several witches were arguing about the best way to fix the painting.

60
00:03:57.149 --> 00:04:02.010
"We should start at the bottom and work our way to the top."

61
00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:05.971
"No! We should start at the top and work our way down."

62
00:04:05.991 --> 00:04:09.472
"I want to add a better finish line," Greta said.

63
00:04:09.492 --> 00:04:11.113
"No way!"

64
00:04:11.453 --> 00:04:12.293
Winnie called out.

65
00:04:12.313 --> 00:04:15.394
"We're not making any changes, you guys.

66
00:04:15.914 --> 00:04:19.135
As soon as the paint is ready, we'll just patch up what we can."

67
00:04:19.155 --> 00:04:23.136
"I think I'll focus on the investigation for now," Ben thought.

68
00:04:23.916 --> 00:04:25.757
He drifted away from the witches again.

69
00:04:25.777 --> 00:04:28.819
"Let's see," he murmured.

70
00:04:28.839 --> 00:04:32.901
"The vandal probably slipped out the gym's rear door."

71
00:04:34.202 --> 00:04:38.905
As Ben floated toward the back of the room, an object under the bleachers caught his eye.

72
00:04:42.207 --> 00:04:43.287
Ben stooped down.

73
00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:49.171
Pixel's camera."

74
00:04:52.012 --> 00:04:55.693
Ben looked around the gym, but he didn't see the younger ghost anywhere.

75
00:04:55.713 --> 00:04:58.294
"That's odd," Ben thought.

76
00:04:58.854 --> 00:05:02.235
Pixel had come to the gym to take photos of the flying painting.

77
00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.056
So why wasn't he here?

78
00:05:04.716 --> 00:05:06.676
And why did he abandon his camera?

79
00:05:07.837 --> 00:05:11.158
Ben turned on the camera and started looking at the photos.

80
00:05:13.359 --> 00:05:17.920
The most recent ones showed the witches' painting—looking absolutely perfect.

81
00:05:21.184 --> 00:05:25.106
"So Pixel was here before the vandal struck," Ben thought.

82
00:05:25.126 --> 00:05:31.368
"I wonder if the vandal was chasing him and that's how Pixel dropped his camera."

83
00:05:32.329 --> 00:05:34.430
Ben suddenly felt very worried.

84
00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:39.652
He didn't know Pixel well, but he did know that the ghost loved his camera.

85
00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:45.154
There was no way Pixel would abandon his camera unless something terrible had happened.

86
00:05:45.975 --> 00:05:48.696
Ben froze, the camera still in his hands.

87
00:05:49.544 --> 00:05:53.169
Where would Pixel go if he needed to hide or get away from someone?

88
00:05:53.189 --> 00:05:58.014
"The old photography classroom!"

89
00:05:58.275 --> 00:05:58.915
Ben thought.

90
00:05:59.356 --> 00:06:03.461
It was a tiny room upstairs, which nobody ever used anymore.

91
00:06:04.222 --> 00:06:05.863
Ben needed to get there right away!
